'''Unifar Temple''' was the home to the [[King]] of the [[planet]] [[Onderon]] during the [[Clone Wars]].

==Description==
The Unifar Temple was located on the [[planet]] [[Onderon]], specifically in the [[capital]] [[city]] of [[Iziz]]. It was surrounded by smaller buildings on three sides, with the remaining side being a wide series of stairs that descended into [[Yolahn Square]]. There were two main pyramidal towers that made the temple have a distinct shape. The Unifar Temple was [[Color|blue]], yellow, and gray in color.<ref name="Two Fronts" /><ref name="Soft War">{{TCW|The Soft War}}</ref>

==History==
The royal palace was the seat of power on Onderon. During the [[Clone Wars]], it was home to [[King]] [[Ramsis Dendup]], who was deposed in a [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]]-backed coup by [[Sanjay Rash]].<ref name="Two Fronts" /> After a successful campaign by the [[Onderon rebels]], the Separatist occupation of the planet was defeated, Rash was killed by the Separatists, and Dendup returned to power, aligning Onderon with the Republic.<ref name="Tipping Points" />

{{Struct-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Iziz royal palace first appeared in the [[1993]] [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] [[Star Wars comic books|comic book]] series ''[[Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi – Ulic Qel-Droma and the Beast Wars of Onderon]]''.<ref name="Two Fronts Trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/a-war-on-two-fronts-trivia-gallery|text="A War on Two Fronts" Trivia Gallery}}</ref> The palace was used in additional Legends media, including the [[2004]] video game ''[[Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic II: The Sith Lords]]''.<ref name="KOTOR2">''[[Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic II: The Sith Lords]]''</ref> The palace was brought into [[canon]] in "[[A War on Two Fronts]]," the second episode of the [[The Clone Wars: Season Five|fifth season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''.<ref name="Two Fronts" />

